Login Success Response

A successful login returns the following fields:

•       token — the signed JWT string

•       tokenType — always "Bearer"

•       expiresAtUtc — UTC timestamp when the token expires

•       user — object containing id, email, and roles array

 
6. How the Client Uses the Token

The client stores the received token and attaches it to every subsequent request for protected endpoints via the Authorization header:

Authorization: Bearer <token>

 
Token Validation Outcomes

•       If token is valid → API allows access to [Authorize] endpoints

•       If token is invalid or expired → API returns 401 Unauthorized

 

 

 

